  "normal_release_byte_identical_to_preceding_main": true,
  "problem": "C127 clocked only the ViewColumns.read cold loader. C128 confirmed that held C116 material-mask queries bypass it, yielding zero View-loader cost for basalt/blackstone despite real Planner.column work. Earlier-height-prefix queries also bypass that View helper in main and candidate. Old results retain their narrow scope and are not evidence that all column cost vanished.",
  "implementation": "Clock the common Planner.column entry instead. For each selected anchor, only an outermost column call creates a span; recursive calls within that anchor fold into it without clocks or duplicate CPU. Nested selected anchors may create their own spans, and direct-child anchor inclusive CPU is subtracted from the parent exactly once. All original commands, ordering, storage and owner lifetimes are unchanged.",
  "scope": "Deterministic 1/64 selected (executed root,x,z) anchors, two salts. Numerator is outermost Planner.column own calling-thread CPU; denominator is own CPU of the same selected anchors including zero-load/empty initializers. Includes direct material-mask and earlier-height entry paths in consumers that use them, ready planner-state lookups and reconstruction. View cache hits and material/derived-mask callbacks after the planner return remain outside. No extrapolation to all anchors/process CPU/wall; observer work is included.",
